---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="INTERFASE: The Infinite Set — Book by Julian Perez"
  description="INTERFASE: The Infinite Set is the debut book by Spanish DJ and producer Julian Perez. A narrative essay on music, career, identity and life on the road — from Ibiza's underground to international festivals. Available in English and Spanish."
>
  <main style="font-family:sans-serif;color:#111;line-height:1.8;">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section style="background:#1a1e5e;color:#fff;padding:5rem 2rem;">
      <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4rem;align-items:center;">
        <div>
          <nav style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
            <a href="/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5);text-decoration:none;font-size:0.85rem;letter-spacing:0.05em;">← julianperez.com</a>
          </nav>
          <p style="color:#4fc8c8;font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:1rem;">Julian Perez — Debut Book · 2026</p>
          <h1 style="font-size:3rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.05;margin:0 0 0.5rem;letter-spacing:-0.02em;">INTERFASE</h1>
          <p style="font-size:1.2rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);margin:0 0 2rem;font-style:italic;">The Infinite Set</p>
          <p style="font-size:1rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">A narrative essay on music, career, identity and the invisible labour behind every set. From the underground clubs of Valencia and Ibiza to international festivals — what you don't see from the outside.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/8409813726" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:inline-block;background:#4fc8c8;color:#1a1e5e;font-weight:700;font-size:0.8rem;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none;padding:0.85rem 1.75rem;border-radius:2px;">Buy in English →</a>
            <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/8409794535" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:inline-block;background:transparent;color:#fff;font-weight:700;font-size:0.8rem;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none;padding:0.85rem 1.75rem;border-radius:2px;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);">Versión en español →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;">
          <img src="/interfase-cover-en.png" alt="INTERFASE: The Infinite Set — book cover by Julian Perez" style="max-width:280px;width:100%;border-radius:4px;box-shadow:0 24px 64px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ABOUT -->
    <section style="padding:5rem 2rem;background:#fff;">
      <div style="max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;">
        <h2 style="font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#999;margin-bottom:2rem;">About the book</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;color:#222;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"><em>INTERFASE</em> is not a success manual, nor a conventional autobiography. It is an honest, intimate — and at times raw — account of what happens when passion has no shortcuts and no guarantees.</p>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.85;color:#444;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">There are stages that cannot be told in order. Internal places without names. Processes that follow no pattern but leave a mark. This book is written not from certainty or success, but from transit: that uncomfortable, fertile space where you are no longer who you were, but don't yet know who you are becoming.</p>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.85;color:#444;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">It is a book about music, yes — but above all about life: about respecting timing, holding doubt, accepting change, and learning to pause. From the first steps in the underground scene to international festivals, Julian Perez shares for the first time what is not visible from the outside: the silent exhaustion, the loyalty to instinct, and the strange beauty of not arriving anywhere, but continuing anyway.</p>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.85;color:#444;">No formulas. Small, uncomfortable, sincere truths. Because sometimes it's not about moving forward — it's about holding on.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EXCERPTS -->
    <section style="padding:5rem 2rem;background:#f7f7f5;">
      <div style="max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;">
        <h2 style="font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#999;margin-bottom:3rem;">From the book</h2>

        <blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #1a1e5e;padding:0 0 0 2rem;margin:0 0 3.5rem;color:#222;">
          <p style="font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-style:italic;">"When you've been a resident DJ and you carry thousands of mixes inside you, when you've improvised in a thousand rooms, that's already part of you. You don't force it, you don't fake it. It's instinct. You've learned to build an atmosphere from nothing, to watch the floor fill up, to keep it warm without losing the thread. And that, believe me, is an art. One you can't learn in a tutorial. You earn it with hours. With mistakes. With skin. That's when I understand Senna. When you enter a state where you don't think. You just are. And everything flows."</p>
        </blockquote>

        <blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #1a1e5e;padding:0 0 0 2rem;margin:0 0 3.5rem;color:#222;">
          <p style="font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-style:italic;">"I learned that I don't want to fill a room if that means emptying myself. That I'd rather play for twenty people who understand what I'm doing and give me the chance to express myself than be at a massive festival forcing something that doesn't represent me. Not everything that moves, advances. Sometimes it just goes in circles. Being true to who you are doesn't always get you likes, or contracts. But it gives you peace. And at this point, that's worth more to me than anything."</p>
        </blockquote>

        <blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #1a1e5e;padding:0 0 0 2rem;margin:0 0 3.5rem;color:#222;">
          <p style="font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-style:italic;">"I'll never forget a gig in Barcelona where they paid me with dinner. No fee, no contract, nothing. The promoter gave me a plate of pasta and a couple of drinks like it was the greatest prize. And even though I laughed inside, the truth is that night I learned more than at many other events: how to build a set with broken equipment, how to hold on when nobody's watching, how to enjoy it even when you're playing out of pure love for the craft. If you can't give everything under those conditions, you won't do it at a festival with ten thousand people either."</p>
        </blockquote>

        <blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #1a1e5e;padding:0 0 0 2rem;margin:0 0 3.5rem;color:#222;">
          <p style="font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-style:italic;">"I've been in booths surrounded by people, smiles, hugs, messages — and gone back to the hotel feeling more alone than ever. I've been at home with one friend, having coffee in silence — and felt truly accompanied. The most important things don't come out in photos or interviews. There are processes nobody applauds, decisions made in silence, sacrifices that lose part of their truth the moment you tell them."</p>
        </blockquote>

        <blockquote style="border-left:3px solid #1a1e5e;padding:0 0 0 2rem;margin:0 0 0;color:#222;">
          <p style="font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-style:italic;">"It's curious: when you stop chasing something, things start to appear on their own. Not because the universe conspires, not because of any cheap mysticism — but because you no longer project that desperation. You work with more calm. You're more centred. And that shows. The rest comes by itself."</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EDITORIAL REVIEW -->
    <section style="padding:5rem 2rem;background:#1a1e5e;color:#fff;">
      <div style="max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;">
        <p style="font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4fc8c8;margin-bottom:2rem;">Editorial review</p>
        <p style="font-size:1.25rem;line-height:1.85;font-style:italic;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">"A work of enormous literary value for its originality, its direct and unguarded style, sober and without pretence. A magnificent book built on a voice of its own — with great expressive force and poetic beauty — that not only grips through its concise narrative but makes us reflect on the complexities of the creative life, success, the vertiginousness of the world, and the need to look inward."</p>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.45);letter-spacing:0.05em;">— Editorial Letra Minúscula · Reader's Report, 2025</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EDITIONS -->
    <section style="padding:5rem 2rem;background:#fff;">
      <div style="max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;">
        <h2 style="font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#999;margin-bottom:3rem;">Editions</h2>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem;">
          <div style="border:1px solid #eee;border-radius:4px;padding:2rem;">
            <img src="/interfase-cover-en.png" alt="INTERFASE: The Infinite Set — English edition" style="width:100%;max-width:120px;display:block;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;border-radius:2px;" />
            <p style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#999;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">English</p>
            <p style="font-weight:700;font-size:1rem;margin:0 0 0.25rem;">INTERFASE: The Infinite Set</p>
            <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#888;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">Julian Perez · 2026 · ISBN 978-8409813728</p>
            <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/8409813726" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:block;text-align:center;background:#1a1e5e;color:#fff;font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none;padding:0.75rem 1rem;border-radius:2px;">Buy on Amazon →</a>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid #eee;border-radius:4px;padding:2rem;">
            <img src="/interfase-cover-es-sq.png" alt="INTERFASE: La sesión infinita — edición en español" style="width:100%;max-width:120px;display:block;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;border-radius:2px;" />
            <p style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#999;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Español</p>
            <p style="font-weight:700;font-size:1rem;margin:0 0 0.25rem;">INTERFASE: La sesión infinita</p>
            <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#888;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">Julián Pérez · 2026 · ISBN 978-8409794539</p>
            <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/8409794535" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:block;text-align:center;background:#1a1e5e;color:#fff;font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none;padding:0.75rem 1rem;border-radius:2px;">Comprar en Amazon →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ABOUT THE AUTHOR -->
    <section style="padding:5rem 2rem;background:#f7f7f5;border-top:1px solid #eee;">
      <div style="max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;">
        <h2 style="font-size:0.75rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#999;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">About the author</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1rem;line-height:1.85;color:#444;margin-bottom:1rem;">Julian Perez is a Spanish DJ and electronic music producer born in Valencia in 1982. Based in Ibiza since 2006, he has performed at venues and festivals across Europe, Asia, North America and South America, and released music on Raum...musik, VIVa Music, Leftroom, 1Trax and his own labels Fathers &amp; Sons Productions and Girada Unlimited. <em>INTERFASE</em> is his debut book.</p>
        <a href="/" style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#1a1e5e;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0.05em;">← julianperez.com</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
